@startuml state-active-page
!include elvira.iuml
' What: in the continuous view the active page is set by scrolling or by a jump, never both at once, so a jump never loops back through the scroll handler and drawing pins the page.
' Kind: UML state machine diagram. Scope: who may change docStore.activePage in the PageStream redesign.
' Source: src/stores/document.ts, src/components/pdf-viewer-page/PageStream.vue (2026-11-18)

title Who owns the active page (proposal, 2026-11-18)

[*] --> Following : document opened (cause: initial)

state Following : the page nearest the top of the view\nbecomes active (cause: scroll, no history)
state Jumping : goTo(page, cause) scrolls the stream there;\nscroll updates are ignored until it settles
state Pinned : a drawing tool is selected;\nscrolling does not change the active page

Following --> Jumping : link · outline · search · citation · host · history · step
Jumping --> Following : scroll settled on the target
Following --> Pinned : drawing tool picked
Pinned --> Following : back to the pointer tool
Pinned --> Jumping : explicit jump (saves the drawing first)

caption Scrolling only reports (cause scroll, no history entry); jumps scroll and are recorded; while drawing, the page is pinned so autosave keys stay right.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersViewer · docs/diagrams/state-active-page.puml
@enduml
